{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":21663599}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Stage 1 Baselines: VADER and Polyglot (lexicon-based)\n\nEvaluates the two lexicon-based baselines from Cosme & De Leon (2024) under the\n**same conditions** as the fine-tuned XLM-R and mBERT models (Objective 7, H01, H03):\n\n- **Same data and preprocessing:** the Stage 1 dataset, cleaned with the study's\n  `clean_text` (case normalization, repeated-character reduction, Taglish spelling map).\n- **Same splits:** the same 15% held-out test set and the same 5 stratified CV folds\n  (seed 42) as the Stage 1 notebooks. The notebook asserts that the holdout matches.\n- **Same metrics:** accuracy, precision, recall, F1, macro/micro P/R/F1, weighted F1,\n  hamming loss, per-class P/R/F1, and confusion matrices (Ch. III).\n- **Same statistical test:** corrected resampled paired t-test on CV fold scores\n  (macro-F1 primary, plus accuracy), as used for XLM-R vs mBERT.\n\n**Kept from Cosme & De Leon (2024), Sec. 3.2:** reviews are translated to English\nwith Google Translate before scoring, because VADER only supports English and\nPolyglot does not support code-switching.\n\n**Added for this study (4 classes instead of 3):** neither tool outputs \"mixed\", so a\nfixed rule set before any results are seen maps reviews with both positive and negative\nevidence to \"mixed\" (see Config). It is never tuned on the data.\n\n**Not included:** GPT-3 and GPT-3.5 (retired by OpenAI before this study's experiments).\nVADER and Polyglot are sentiment-only tools, so they are Stage 1 baselines only.\n\n**Run order:** finish both Stage 1 notebooks first. This notebook reads their fold\nCSVs and test predictions. No GPU needed. The first run translates all 10,510\nreviews (about 1 to 1.5 hours). It is cached and resumable, so reruns are instant.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Setup","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"!pip install -q vaderSentiment polyglot3 deep-translator scikit-learn matplotlib scipy","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:27:36.426321Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:27:36.427128Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.098677Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:27:36.427102Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.097788Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import os, re, time, unicodedata\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, f1_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n                             hamming_loss, confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.100508Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.100857Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.106112Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.100834Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.105332Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Config (must match the Stage 1 notebooks)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import glob, shutil\n\nINPUT_DIR = os.path.dirname(glob.glob(\"/kaggle/input/**/SentiTaglish_ProductsAndServices.csv\", recursive=True)[0])\nprint(\"INPUT_DIR:\", INPUT_DIR)\nWORK = \"/kaggle/working\"\nDATA_PATH = f\"{INPUT_DIR}/SentiTaglish_ProductsAndServices.csv\"\nHOLDOUT_PATH = f\"{INPUT_DIR}/holdout_test_stage1.csv\"\nTRANSLATION_CACHE = f\"{WORK}/stage1_translated_en.csv\"\nRESULTS_DIR = f\"{WORK}/results\"\nos.makedirs(RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n# Copy Stage 1 result CSVs into the writable folder\nfor f in glob.glob(f\"{INPUT_DIR}/stage1_*.csv\"):\n    shutil.copy(f, RESULTS_DIR)\n\n# Resume translation from an earlier session, if you uploaded the cache\nif os.path.exists(f\"{INPUT_DIR}/stage1_translated_en.csv\") and not os.path.exists(TRANSLATION_CACHE):\n    shutil.copy(f\"{INPUT_DIR}/stage1_translated_en.csv\", TRANSLATION_CACHE)\n\n# Same as Stage 1\nSEED = 42\nTEST_SIZE = 0.15\nN_FOLDS = 5\nLABEL_NAMES = [\"negative\", \"neutral\", \"positive\", \"mixed\"]\nLABEL2ID = {n: i for i, n in enumerate(LABEL_NAMES)}\nIDS = list(range(len(LABEL_NAMES)))\nSENTIMENT_CODE_MAP = {1: \"negative\", 2: \"neutral\", 3: \"positive\", 4: \"mixed\"}\n\n# VADER: standard compound thresholds (Hutto & Gilbert, 2014)\nVADER_POS_T = 0.05\nVADER_NEG_T = -0.05\n# Mixed rule (added for 4 classes): positive AND negative proportions both >= this\nVADER_MIXED_T = 0.10\n\n# Polyglot mixed rule: at least this many positive AND negative words\nPOLYGLOT_MIXED_MIN = 1\n\n# Fine-tuned models (outputs of the Stage 1 notebooks)\nFINETUNED = {\n    \"XLM-R\": \"xlm-roberta-base\",\n    \"mBERT\": \"bert-base-multilingual-uncased\",\n}","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.107179Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.107517Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.13717Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.107486Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.136616Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Preprocessing (identical to the Stage 1 notebooks)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"SPELLING_MAP = {\n    \"d2\": \"dito\", \"dto\": \"dito\",\n    \"un\": \"yun\",\n    \"sya\": \"siya\", \"cya\": \"siya\",\n    \"nde\": \"hindi\", \"hnd\": \"hindi\",\n    \"wla\": \"wala\", \"wlang\": \"walang\",\n    \"eto\": \"ito\",\n    \"pde\": \"pwede\", \"pwd\": \"pwede\",\n    \"gud\": \"good\",\n    \"thnx\": \"thanks\", \"tnx\": \"thanks\",\n    \"salamt\": \"salamat\",\n}\n\n_REPEATED_CHAR = re.compile(r\"(.)\\1{2,}\")\n_WHITESPACE = re.compile(r\"\\s+\")\n\ndef clean_text(text: str) -> str:\n    if not isinstance(text, str) or not text.strip():\n        return \"\"\n    text = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKC\", text)\n    text = text.lower()\n    text = _REPEATED_CHAR.sub(r\"\\1\\1\", text)\n    tokens = text.split()\n    tokens = [SPELLING_MAP.get(t, t) for t in tokens]\n    text = \" \".join(tokens)\n    text = _WHITESPACE.sub(\" \", text).strip()\n    return text","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.138545Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.13886Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.144589Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.138841Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.143906Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Load data and rebuild the Stage 1 splits","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\ndf[\"row_id\"] = np.arange(len(df))\ndf[\"sentiment_label\"] = df[\"sentiment\"].map(SENTIMENT_CODE_MAP)\nassert df[\"sentiment_label\"].notna().all()\ndf[\"label\"] = df[\"sentiment_label\"].map(LABEL2ID)\ndf[\"review_clean\"] = df[\"review\"].apply(clean_text)\ndf = df[df[\"review_clean\"] != \"\"].reset_index(drop=True)\n\ndev_df, test_df = train_test_split(df, test_size=TEST_SIZE, stratify=df[\"label\"], random_state=SEED)\ndev_df, test_df = dev_df.reset_index(drop=True), test_df.reset_index(drop=True)\n\nsaved = pd.read_csv(HOLDOUT_PATH)\nassert sorted(saved[\"row_id\"]) == sorted(test_df[\"row_id\"]), \"Holdout does not match Stage 1\"\nprint(f\"Holdout matches Stage 1 | Dev (CV pool): {len(dev_df)} | Held-out test: {len(test_df)}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.145562Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.146049Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.410847Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.146029Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.410015Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Translate to English (Cosme & De Leon, 2024)\n\nTranslates the cleaned text of every review once. Progress is saved every 50\nreviews, so if Google rate-limits you, just rerun this cell and it resumes.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import torch\nfrom transformers import MarianMTModel, MarianTokenizer\n\nMT_MODEL = \"Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-tl-en\"\ndevice = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\ntok = MarianTokenizer.from_pretrained(MT_MODEL)\nmt = MarianMTModel.from_pretrained(MT_MODEL).to(device).eval()\n\nall_df = pd.concat([dev_df, test_df], ignore_index=True)\ncache = pd.read_csv(TRANSLATION_CACHE) if os.path.exists(TRANSLATION_CACHE) else pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"row_id\", \"review_en\"])\ntodo = all_df[~all_df[\"row_id\"].isin(set(cache[\"row_id\"]))]\nprint(f\"Cached: {len(cache)} | To translate: {len(todo)} | device: {device}\")\n\nBATCH = 64\nids, texts = todo[\"row_id\"].tolist(), todo[\"review_clean\"].tolist()\nfor start in range(0, len(texts), BATCH):\n    batch = texts[start:start + BATCH]\n    enc = tok(batch, return_tensors=\"pt\", padding=True, truncation=True, max_length=256).to(device)\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        out = mt.generate(**enc, max_length=256, num_beams=4)\n    en_batch = tok.batch_decode(out, skip_special_tokens=True)\n    pd.DataFrame({\"row_id\": ids[start:start + BATCH], \"review_en\": en_batch}).to_csv(\n        TRANSLATION_CACHE, mode=\"a\", header=not os.path.exists(TRANSLATION_CACHE), index=False)\n    if (start // BATCH) % 20 == 0:\n        print(f\"  {start + len(batch)}/{len(texts)} translated\")\n\ncache = pd.read_csv(TRANSLATION_CACHE).drop_duplicates(\"row_id\", keep=\"last\")\nen = dict(zip(cache[\"row_id\"], cache[\"review_en\"].fillna(\"\")))\ndev_df[\"review_en\"] = dev_df[\"row_id\"].map(en)\ntest_df[\"review_en\"] = test_df[\"row_id\"].map(en)\nassert dev_df[\"review_en\"].notna().all() and test_df[\"review_en\"].notna().all()\nprint(test_df[[\"review_clean\", \"review_en\"]].head(10).to_string())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.412009Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.412328Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:38.58479Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:27:38.412296Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:38.583996Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6. VADER","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from vaderSentiment.vaderSentiment import SentimentIntensityAnalyzer\nvader = SentimentIntensityAnalyzer()\n\ndef vader_label(text):\n    s = vader.polarity_scores(text)\n    if s[\"pos\"] >= VADER_MIXED_T and s[\"neg\"] >= VADER_MIXED_T:\n        return \"mixed\"\n    if s[\"compound\"] >= VADER_POS_T:\n        return \"positive\"\n    if s[\"compound\"] <= VADER_NEG_T:\n        return \"negative\"\n    return \"neutral\"\n\nfor d in (dev_df, test_df):\n    d[\"pred_vader\"] = d[\"review_en\"].apply(vader_label)\nprint(test_df[\"pred_vader\"].value_counts())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:38.585912Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:38.586255Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:39.512506Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:38.586231Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:39.511889Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Polyglot\n\nDownloads the English sentiment lexicon once (`sentiment2.en`). Each word is\nscored +1, 0, or -1.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from polyglot3.downloader import downloader\nfrom polyglot3.text import Text\n\nok = downloader.download(\"sentiment2.en\", quiet=True)\nassert ok, \"Polyglot lexicon download failed. Check your internet connection and rerun.\"\n\ndef polyglot_label(text):\n    if not isinstance(text, str) or not text.strip():\n        return \"neutral\"\n    try:\n        pols = [w.polarity for w in Text(text, hint_language_code=\"en\").words]\n    except Exception:\n        return \"neutral\"\n    n_pos = sum(p > 0 for p in pols)\n    n_neg = sum(p < 0 for p in pols)\n    if n_pos >= POLYGLOT_MIXED_MIN and n_neg >= POLYGLOT_MIXED_MIN:\n        return \"mixed\"\n    if n_pos > n_neg:\n        return \"positive\"\n    if n_neg > n_pos:\n        return \"negative\"\n    return \"neutral\"\n\nfor d in (dev_df, test_df):\n    d[\"pred_polyglot\"] = d[\"review_en\"].apply(polyglot_label)\nprint(test_df[\"pred_polyglot\"].value_counts())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:39.513441Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:39.514011Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.119249Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:39.513977Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.118253Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 8. Metrics (Ch. III)\n\nSame metric set as the Stage 1 notebooks, plus per-class precision/recall and\nhamming loss. For single-label classification, hamming loss equals 1 - accuracy\nand micro-P/R/F1 equal accuracy.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def score(y_true, y_pred):\n    y = [LABEL2ID[v] for v in y_true]\n    p = [LABEL2ID[v] for v in y_pred]\n    kw = dict(labels=IDS, zero_division=0)\n    row = {\n        \"accuracy\": accuracy_score(y, p),\n        \"macro_f1\": f1_score(y, p, average=\"macro\", **kw),\n        \"micro_f1\": f1_score(y, p, average=\"micro\", **kw),\n        \"weighted_f1\": f1_score(y, p, average=\"weighted\", **kw),\n        \"macro_precision\": precision_score(y, p, average=\"macro\", **kw),\n        \"micro_precision\": precision_score(y, p, average=\"micro\", **kw),\n        \"macro_recall\": recall_score(y, p, average=\"macro\", **kw),\n        \"micro_recall\": recall_score(y, p, average=\"micro\", **kw),\n        \"hamming_loss\": hamming_loss(y, p),\n    }\n    for metric, fn in [(\"precision\", precision_score), (\"recall\", recall_score), (\"f1\", f1_score)]:\n        for name, v in zip(LABEL_NAMES, fn(y, p, average=None, **kw)):\n            row[f\"{metric}_{name}\"] = v\n    return row","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.120298Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.120664Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.127409Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.120631Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.12656Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 9. Cross-validation scores (same 5 folds as Stage 1)\n\nThe lexicon tools are not trained, so each fold's score is simply the tool's\nscore on that fold's validation reviews. This makes them directly comparable\nwith the XLM-R and mBERT fold scores.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"skf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=N_FOLDS, shuffle=True, random_state=SEED)\nfold_rows = {\"vader\": [], \"polyglot\": []}\nfor fold, (tr, va) in enumerate(skf.split(dev_df, dev_df[\"label\"])):\n    v = dev_df.iloc[va]\n    for tag in fold_rows:\n        fold_rows[tag].append({\"model\": tag, \"fold\": fold, **score(v[\"sentiment_label\"], v[f\"pred_{tag}\"])})\n\nfor tag, rows in fold_rows.items():\n    res = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    res.to_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_{tag}_folds.csv\", index=False)\n    print(f\"\\n{tag.upper()} CV (mean, std):\")\n    print(res.drop(columns=[\"model\", \"fold\"]).describe().loc[[\"mean\", \"std\"]].round(4).T)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.129807Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.130012Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.5049Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.129994Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.504298Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 10. Held-out test results and confusion matrices","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def save_confusion(y_true, y_pred, tag, title):\n    cm = confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred, labels=LABEL_NAMES)\n    pd.DataFrame(cm, index=[f\"true_{n}\" for n in LABEL_NAMES],\n                 columns=[f\"pred_{n}\" for n in LABEL_NAMES]).to_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_{tag}_test_confusion.csv\")\n    ConfusionMatrixDisplay(cm, display_labels=LABEL_NAMES).plot(cmap=\"Blues\")\n    plt.title(title)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_{tag}_test_confusion.png\", dpi=200)\n    plt.show()\n\nfor tag, title in [(\"vader\", \"VADER\"), (\"polyglot\", \"Polyglot\")]:\n    s = score(test_df[\"sentiment_label\"], test_df[f\"pred_{tag}\"])\n    pd.DataFrame([{\"model\": tag, **s}]).to_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_{tag}_test.csv\", index=False)\n    out = test_df[[\"row_id\", \"review\", \"review_en\", \"sentiment_label\"]].copy()\n    out[\"pred_label\"] = test_df[f\"pred_{tag}\"]\n    out.to_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_{tag}_test_predictions.csv\", index=False)\n    print(f\"\\n{title} held-out test results:\")\n    print(pd.Series(s).round(4))\n    save_confusion(test_df[\"sentiment_label\"], test_df[f\"pred_{tag}\"], tag, f\"Stage 1 held-out test ({title})\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.505731Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.50596Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.387879Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:42.50594Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.387312Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 11. All models on the held-out test set\n\nRecomputes every model's metrics from its saved predictions with the same\n`score()` function, so all rows use identical metric code.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"preds = {\n    \"Polyglot\": test_df[[\"row_id\", \"sentiment_label\", \"pred_polyglot\"]].rename(columns={\"pred_polyglot\": \"pred_label\"}),\n    \"VADER\": test_df[[\"row_id\", \"sentiment_label\", \"pred_vader\"]].rename(columns={\"pred_vader\": \"pred_label\"}),\n}\nfor name, tag in FINETUNED.items():\n    d = pd.read_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_{tag}_test_predictions.csv\")[[\"row_id\", \"sentiment_label\", \"pred_label\"]]\n    assert sorted(d[\"row_id\"]) == sorted(test_df[\"row_id\"]), f\"{name} was not evaluated on this holdout\"\n    preds[name] = d\n\norder = [\"Polyglot\", \"VADER\", \"mBERT\", \"XLM-R\"]\ntable = pd.DataFrame([{\"model\": m, **score(preds[m][\"sentiment_label\"], preds[m][\"pred_label\"])} for m in order])\ntable.to_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_all_models_test.csv\", index=False)\n\nmain_cols = [\"model\", \"accuracy\", \"macro_f1\", \"micro_f1\", \"weighted_f1\",\n             \"macro_precision\", \"macro_recall\", \"hamming_loss\"]\nprint(\"Overall:\")\nprint(table[main_cols].round(4).to_string(index=False))\nfor metric in [\"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\"]:\n    print(f\"\\nPer-class {metric}:\")\n    print(table[[\"model\"] + [f\"{metric}_{n}\" for n in LABEL_NAMES]].round(4).to_string(index=False))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.38891Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.389248Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.537799Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.389226Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.537163Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Reference only: Cosme & De Leon (2024), Table 4. Different task (3 classes, no\n# \"mixed\") and a different test split, so not directly comparable.\ncosme = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"model\": [\"Polyglot\", \"VADER\", \"mBERT\", \"XLM-R\", \"GPT-3\", \"GPT-3.5\"],\n    \"accuracy\": [0.51, 0.57, 0.82, 0.84, 0.77, 0.74],\n    \"weighted_f1\": [0.49, 0.50, 0.82, 0.84, 0.78, 0.71],\n})\nprint(\"Cosme & De Leon (2024), 3-class FiReCS, for reference:\")\nprint(cosme.to_string(index=False))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.538518Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.538755Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.545652Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.538735Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.544797Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 12. Hypothesis tests: XLM-R vs each baseline (H01, H03)\n\nSame method as the XLM-R vs mBERT comparison: corrected resampled paired t-test\n(Nadeau & Bengio, 2003) on the 5 CV fold scores. Macro-F1 is the primary metric;\naccuracy and weighted-F1 are also tested (H03 covers macro-F1 and accuracy).\nHolm correction is applied across the three baselines for each metric.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def corrected_ttest(a, b, n_train, n_test):\n    d = np.asarray(a) - np.asarray(b)\n    k = len(d)\n    t = d.mean() / np.sqrt((1 / k + n_test / n_train) * d.var(ddof=1))\n    p = 2 * stats.t.sf(abs(t), df=k - 1)\n    return t, p\n\ndef holm(pvals):\n    p = np.asarray(pvals); order = np.argsort(p); m = len(p)\n    adj = np.empty(m); running = 0.0\n    for rank, idx in enumerate(order):\n        running = max(running, min(1.0, (m - rank) * p[idx]))\n        adj[idx] = running\n    return adj\n\nN_TEST = round(len(dev_df) / N_FOLDS)      # 1787\nN_TRAIN = len(dev_df) - N_TEST              # 7146\n\nfolds = {\n    \"XLM-R\": pd.read_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_xlm-roberta-base_folds.csv\"),\n    \"mBERT\": pd.read_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_bert-base-multilingual-uncased_folds.csv\"),\n    \"VADER\": pd.read_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_vader_folds.csv\"),\n    \"Polyglot\": pd.read_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_polyglot_folds.csv\"),\n}\nfolds = {k: v.sort_values(\"fold\").reset_index(drop=True) for k, v in folds.items()}\n\nrows = []\nfor metric in [\"macro_f1\", \"accuracy\", \"weighted_f1\"]:\n    block = []\n    for base in [\"mBERT\", \"VADER\", \"Polyglot\"]:\n        a, b = folds[\"XLM-R\"][metric], folds[base][metric]\n        t, p = corrected_ttest(a, b, N_TRAIN, N_TEST)\n        block.append({\"metric\": metric, \"comparison\": f\"XLM-R vs {base}\",\n                      \"xlmr_mean\": a.mean(), \"baseline_mean\": b.mean(), \"t\": t, \"p\": p})\n    for r, ph in zip(block, holm([r[\"p\"] for r in block])):\n        r[\"p_holm\"] = ph\n        r[\"significant\"] = ph < 0.05\n    rows += block\n\ntests = pd.DataFrame(rows)\ntests.to_csv(f\"{RESULTS_DIR}/stage1_hypothesis_tests.csv\", index=False)\nprint(tests.round(4).to_string(index=False))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.5472Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.547493Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.578091Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.547473Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:42:43.577458Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import shutil\nshutil.copy(\"/kaggle/working/stage1_translated_en.csv\", \"/kaggle/working/results/\")\nshutil.make_archive(\"/kaggle/working/stage1_baselines_results\", \"zip\", \"/kaggle/working/results\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-04T08:48:48.400741Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-04T08:48:48.401156Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-04T08:48:48.592849Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-04T08:48:48.401128Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-04T08:48:48.592105Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":38,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"'/kaggle/working/stage1_baselines_results.zip'"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":38}]}